{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c3","c4"],"primary":"c3","title":"Berkeley Rent Stabilization and Eviction for Just Cause Ordinance: just cause eviction requirements (as amended by Measure BB)","requirement":"Landlords cannot evict tenants in fully or partially covered units without just cause, and Measure BB tightened the grounds and notice rules. For example, a nonpayment eviction requires rental debt of at least one month of HUD Fair Market Rent, termination notices must be filed with the Rent Board within three business days of service, and owner move-in evictions require inflation-indexed relocation assistance.","key_value":"Nonpayment eviction only if rental debt is at least one month of HUD Fair Market Rent (Oakland-Fremont HUD Metro FMR) for an equivalent-size unit. Termination notices, notices to quit and summons/complaints must be filed with the Rent Board within 3 business days of service. Owner move-in relocation payments from 2026-01-01: standard $19,413; additional payment for qualifying households $6,471 (a 1.5% CPI-U increase).","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Stabilization and Eviction for Just Cause Ordinance (also cited as the Rent Stabilization and Good Cause for Eviction Ordinance), as amended by Measure BB (Nov. 2024)","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units: most multifamily buildings built before 1980, single-family homes with tenancies that began before 1996, and rooming houses. Partially covered units: new construction with a Certificate of Occupancy issued after June 1980, single-family homes with tenancies beginning on or after January 1, 1996, and most condominiums. Owner move-in relocation assistance applies to tenants evicted for an owner move-in.","exemptions":"Exempt units: Section 202 and Section 811 subsidized units; units with Rental Supplement, Section 8 Loan Management Set Aside or Project-based Section 8 subsidies in a project with a HUD-insured or HUD-held mortgage; 'Golden Duplex' units; units where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath with the owner; tenancies started after Nov 7, 2018 on properties with an ADU where either unit is owner-occupied; university rental units such as dormitories; nonprofit cooperatives.","coverage_from":"c4","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2"],"primary":"c2","title":"Berkeley Ellis Implementation Ordinance: Ellis Act relocation assistance","requirement":"Owners who evict tenants to remove a property from the rental housing market must pay the same relocation assistance as for an owner move-in eviction. The payments are indexed to inflation, and the Rent Board publishes the yearly increases.","key_value":"From 2026-01-01: standard relocation payment $19,413; additional payment for qualifying households $6,471 (a 1.5% increase).","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Ellis Implementation Ordinance","coverage_conditions":"Tenants evicted so the owner can remove the property from the rental housing market (Ellis Act evictions).","exemptions":null,"coverage_from":"c2","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
